  "CHARACTER IMAGE": "",
  "AlliesOrganizations": "=== Allies === \n\n- Madame Zora. \"The Spider\": She runs a high-end tailoring shop in Neverwinter. She dresses the nobility but sells their secrets. She knew Aedric (Malakai's younger brother). She blames Malakai slightly for his death but respects Malakai's skills. \n\n- Aedric Rainstalker (Dead): Malakai’s younger brother. Though deceased, he remains Malakai’s primary \"ally\" in spirit. Malakai often speaks to him under his breath or carries a small, wooden memento of him, which is the last thing that he has left of his brother. \n\n=== Organizations === \n\nHe used to work for House Vaelmont and various criminal organizations, but after his exile from Neverwinter, he is on his own.",
  "PersonalityTraits ": "I always have a plan for what to do when things go wrong. \nI am incredibly slow to trust. Those who seem the fairest often have the",
  "Ideals": "Redemption. I need to make up for the mistake that got Aedric killed. \nJustice. I will find a way to break free",
  "Bonds": "Someone I loved died because of a mistake I made. That will never happen again.",
  "Appearance": "",
  "Flaws": "I have a “tell” that reveals when I’m lying.",
  "Backstory": "Malakai didn’t know much about his parents. He only knew they existed. His father was absent, a Sun Elf, and his mother was a human woman from the Docks District. Any relationship they might've shared with their parents was not long-lasting enough to leave a mark on the two brothers. His mother had been dead long before Aedric could remember what she looked like, and his father had never been present in a manner that actually mattered. By the time he was nine, there was a six-year-old brother crying at night, and a city that couldn't care less whether they ate or not. He made his choices thereafter accordingly. \n\nHe began stealing out of need, then out of sheer talent, proving himself an unusually skilled thief. He was fast, clever, and possessed a talent for making people comfortable with him even as he relieved them of their purses or evaluated what they might lose to him. By his mid-teens, he’d moved from simple theft into working as a courier for one of Dockward’s more established crime syndicates, delivering packages he wisely never opened. By seventeen, he was skilled enough to ride with a real crew, handling the work that required him to pass through the city’s more affluent areas without ever being noticed. \n\nInformation was money to him. Malakai realized from the very beginning that the value of a secret far outweighed the value of the thing or the person it was about. He built his network thoughtfully, strategically placing his informants in the servants' halls, the counting houses, the guilds, only passing on what he needed to, holding the rest in reserve for when it might be useful to him. He didn’t wear an easy smile or idle sentiment. Neverwinter’s underworld didn’t take kindly to sentiment, and he had learnt it the hard way. There was only one thing that might move him. Only one thing that had any chance of getting through to him. And that was his brother. He made sure Aedric was fed. He paid for his education. And he made sure the boy had a room that could",
  "AdditionalNotes1": "- Malakai carries a small hawk charm close to his heart. It has carefully etched lines. In his downtime or when the situation calls for it, he talks to the charm. He whispers the word “Aedric” while recalling the stunning view he just witnessed or the wine he got to taste. This charm is the only thing that drives him forward. It’s the spark that lets him get through another day and stand up for what’s right. \n\n- Malakai wears a thorned collar around his neck. It’s enchanted. It reacts when he speaks negatively about House Vaelmont or acts against their interests. When the thorned collar reacts, it lights up and constricts. It hurts him unless he stops talking. After the reaction subsides, the thorned collar goes back to its original size. However, with each time it happens, the thorned collar constricts a bit more. \n\n- Malakai has acquired a habit when he’s lying. He touches the thorned collar. Although he doesn’t take it off, his hand rubs the cold metal as if bracing for the pain.",
  "AdditionalNotes2": "",
